    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n49118" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">trĭmĕtrŏs</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-trus</span></b> , tra, trum
		(postclass. collat. form <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">trĭmĕtrĭus</span></b> , a,
		um, <i><span class="en">Aus. Ep. 16, 78</span></i>; Sid.
		poët. Ep. 9, 15), adj., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρίμετρος;</span> in prosody, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>containing three metres</i> or <i>double-feet</i>, <i>trimeter</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">versus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Quint. 10, 1, 99</span></i>
			.—As <i>subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">trĭmē^tros</span></b> 
				(<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-trus</span></b> ),
				i, m., <i>a
			trimeter</i>, <i><span class="en">Quint. 9, 4, 90</span></i>; <i><span class="en">9, 4, 75</span></i>; <i><span class="en">9, 4, 108 al.</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Hor. A.
				P. 252</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Ter. Maur. p. 2432</span></i> P.;
					<i><span class="en">Diom. p. 506</span></i>
			ib.—Also called <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">trĭmĕ-ter</span></b> ,
				<i><span class="en">Serv. Verg. E. 8, 78</span></i>.</div>
